  "body": "From the high-tier review of PR #1019 (#994), non-blocking notes: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/1019 (review at 321df394). Both are latent today (the generators never produce these streams) but would post a traverse lower than a hop on a foreign or legacy stream:\n\n1. **Two cycle records with no rapid between them.** `cycleSeat` positions XY at the current Z, which is R after a `G99` hole. So a stream that goes straight from one cycle record to the next with no leaving rapid traverses between holes at R. That is what such a stream literally says, but it is the R-plane traverse #994 removed. Expected: refuse it by name, or seat via the section's `RetractPlane` (the hop) before moving over the next hole.\n2. **`seatKnown` after probing.** `onProbeMove` and the protected probe moves do not set `seatKnown`, so a cycle after probing in the same section is not seated.\n\nApplies to the six canned-cycle mill posts (fanuc, haas, mazak, sinumerik, tormach, doosan-dnm), and to fanuc-lathe's face cycles once #1025/#1026 land.\n\n**Done means:** both cases either seat by the hop law or refuse by name; each is pinned with the #994 `cycle_hop` checker on a synthetic stream on all six posts; goldens are unchanged, since no generator emits these streams.\n\nStack on #1019 (and #1002) while they are open.\n",
